{{!
Local override of openapi-generator's bundled asciidoc model.mustache
(github.com/OpenAPITools/openapi-generator, v7.24.0, modules/openapi-generator/
src/main/resources/asciidoc/model.mustache), wired in via
clients/asciidoc/conf.json's "templateDir". This is a Mustache comment, so it
produces no output -- see the enum-values table further down for the actual
change, flagged with an inline comment there.

Summary: the enum-values row's tablecellcontent-wrapped value lookup can't
resolve that lambda from inside the enum-values iteration, because each
iteration's context there is a raw string, not a map/bean -- so the lookup
doesn't walk up to the parent context and throws NullPointerException: Null
context for variable 'tablecellcontent', which aborts the whole index.adoc
generation. Confirmed via openapi-generator issue #12266, a same-root-cause
bug report against this exact model.mustache enum-rendering code path.
Dropping the lambda for this one row means enum values print unescaped,
which only matters if a value contains a literal pipe character (breaks an
AsciiDoc table cell) -- not a concern for this spec's enums (plain
identifiers). Everything else in this file is untouched, byte-for-byte from
upstream.
}}
